{
  "version": 1,
  "generator": "tests/story_bench.c (make story)",
  "policy": "An operator who reads the panel, not the code: each night it starts at the setting written in the kept logbooks, or at a hunch two steps either side of the nearest setting; it fires, pools the shots fired at one setting, and seals when the pooled share is within 0.6-1.4 x the band's half width of the target, loosening by a quarter with every further shot there; otherwise it turns the dial one step toward the target, re-reads the closer of two settings that point at each other, and never re-seals a setting the check rejected. It does not wait for a full battery and does not know the solver's share. Its hand comes from the run's own stirred seed, re-drawn per night. Choices follow the path field.",
  "crisis": "a shot fired with the battery in the red (below 3 shots left), an empty battery, or a failure (a failure counts as a crisis)",
  "failure": "a seal the check rejected, or an empty battery while the line still stood (an hour on the generator)",
  "segments": ["night 1: half", "night 2: a quarter", "night 3: seven in ten", "night 4: one in eight", "night 5: half, alone"],
  "note": "16 seeds x 12 runs; every run has its own stirred seed; the path comes from the run number.",
